From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: dram: h616: give the display engine MBUS port priority

A 4096x2160 60 Hz scanout (594 MHz pixel clock, 304 pixels of
horizontal blanking) leaves the DE little time to refill its line
buffer. With the video engine decoding 4K HEVC at the same time, the
TCON TV FIFO underflowed 39 to 58 times in 30 seconds and the screen
showed displaced lines. With the priority bit of port 16 (DE) set: no
underflow in 60 seconds each at 4096x2160 59.94/60 Hz and 3840x2160
60 Hz under the same decode, DE clock 600 MHz.

Set the priority bit of port 16, as already done for port 25.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@
 	MBUS_CONF(8, false,    HIGH, 0,  256,  128,   64);
 	MBUS_CONF(11, false,    HIGH, 0,  256,  128,  100);
 	MBUS_CONF(14, false,    HIGH, 0, 1024,  256,   64);
-	MBUS_CONF(16, false, HIGHEST, 6, 8192, 2800, 2400);
+	MBUS_CONF(16,  true, HIGHEST, 6, 8192, 2800, 2400);
 	MBUS_CONF(21, false, HIGHEST, 6, 2048,  768,  512);
 	MBUS_CONF(22, false,    HIGH, 0,  256,  128,  100);
 	MBUS_CONF(25, true,  HIGHEST, 0,  100,   64,   32);
